[break] the-mouse-left-on-at-the-end
rule: Putting the terminal back turns mouse reporting off before it leaves the alternate screen.
file: crates/cortex-term/src/terminal.rs
in: Terminal::end
find: end.extend_from_slice(MOUSE_OFF);
replace: end.extend_from_slice(b"");
caught-by:
    cortex-term terminal::tests::the_mouse_is_on_only_with_the_alternate_screen_and_off_on_every_way_out

[break] the-mouse-left-on-with-the-main-screen
rule: Leaving the alternate screen turns mouse reporting off with it.
file: crates/cortex-term/src/terminal.rs
in: Terminal::alternate
find: bytes.extend_from_slice(MOUSE_OFF);
replace: bytes.extend_from_slice(b"");
caught-by:
    cortex-term terminal::tests::the_mouse_is_on_only_with_the_alternate_screen_and_off_on_every_way_out

[break] the-emergency-restore-leaves-the-mouse-on
rule: Every emergency restore with the alternate screen on turns mouse reporting off.
file: crates/cortex-term/src/sys/mod.rs
